 Personal site of BRKMYR: AI platforms, data platforms, the rise of Physical AI, agentic AI, product innovation. A single static page, no build step, no dependencies, no tracking. The one script is an inline canvas background that degrades to nothing.
 
 Live data, kept honest: the corner readouts show real hub-city clocks (computed client-side), a real measured ping (timed same-origin favicon fetch), and real current temperatures from Open-Meteo. That weather request is the page's single external call: keyless, read-only, no visitor data beyond the request itself. Market tickers are simulated ambience; live quotes would need a keyed API.
+The gate page can reach further, and only on request: the live dashboard loads from its Space after a click on the poster.
 
 Link-only visibility: the page carries a robots noindex tag, and the owner's name appears in the source only entity-encoded. Keep both when editing.
